IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- sections 10 to 14: survival of causes of action on death, loss of expectation of life, interest on debts and
-- damages, charges over choses in action, and the husband's liability.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer".

§ `Section 10 -- effect of death on certain causes of action`

-- src:972 | 10.—(1) Subject to this section, on the death of any person, all
-- src:973 | causes of action subsisting against or vested in him shall survive
-- src:974 | against, or, as the case may be, for the benefit of his estate.
@ref s 10(1) (src:972-974)
GIVEN `the cause of action subsisted against or was vested in the person at the time of his death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of cause of action` IS A `Kind of cause of action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1) the cause of action survives against or for the benefit of the estate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause of action subsisted against or was vested in the person at the time of his death` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all causes of action subsisting against or vested in him"
        IF `the kind of cause of action` EQUALS Defamation OR `the kind of cause of action` EQUALS Seduction OR `the kind of cause of action` EQUALS `Inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other` OR `the kind of cause of action` EQUALS `A claim for damages on the ground of adultery` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this section" -- subsection (2) takes these four out; see s 10(2)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:976 | (2) Subsection (1) shall not apply to causes of action for defamation
-- src:977 | or seduction or for inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from
-- src:978 | the other or to any claim for damages on the ground of adultery.
@ref s 10(2) (src:976-978)
GIVEN `the kind of cause of action` IS A `Kind of cause of action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) subsection (1) applies to the cause of action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of cause of action` EQUALS Defamation OR `the kind of cause of action` EQUALS Seduction OR `the kind of cause of action` EQUALS `Inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other` OR `the kind of cause of action` EQUALS `A claim for damages on the ground of adultery` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) shall not apply to causes of action for defamation or seduction or for inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other or to any claim for damages on the ground of adultery"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the four causes of action it takes out and says nothing of any other

-- Hand-gathering function (ruling E1, option B as guidance): one answer for "does the cause of action survive?", reading s 10(2) before s 10(1).
-- src:972 | 10.—(1) Subject to this section, on the death of any person, all
-- src:973 | causes of action subsisting against or vested in him shall survive
-- src:974 | against, or, as the case may be, for the benefit of his estate.
-- src:976 | (2) Subsection (1) shall not apply to causes of action for defamation
-- src:977 | or seduction or for inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from
-- src:978 | the other or to any claim for damages on the ground of adultery.
@ref s 10(1) and (2) gathered (src:972-978)
GIVEN `the cause of action subsisted against or was vested in the person at the time of his death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of cause of action` IS A `Kind of cause of action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 the cause of action survives the death of the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 10(2) subsection (1) applies to the cause of action` `the kind of cause of action`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) shall not apply" (s 10(2))
    OTHERWISE `s 10(1) the cause of action survives against or for the benefit of the estate` `the cause of action subsisted against or was vested in the person at the time of his death` `the kind of cause of action`

-- src:980 | (3) Where a cause of action survives as specified under
-- src:981 | subsection (1) for the benefit of the estate of a deceased person,
-- src:982 | the damages recoverable for the benefit of the estate of that person —
-- src:984 | (a) shall not include —
-- src:986 | (i) any exemplary damages; and
-- src:988 | (ii) any damages for loss of income in respect of any
-- src:989 | period after that person’s death;
@ref s 10(3)(a) (src:980-989)
GIVEN `the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the head of damages` IS A `Head of damages for the benefit of an estate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3)(a) the head of damages is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a cause of action survives as specified under subsection (1) for the benefit of the estate of a deceased person" -- a scope; the damages are not the subject here
        IF `the head of damages` EQUALS `Exemplary damages` OR `the head of damages` EQUALS `Damages for loss of income in respect of a period after the death` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not include — (i) any exemplary damages; and (ii) any damages for loss of income in respect of any period after that person's death"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the damages do not include and says nothing of any other head

-- src:980 | (3) Where a cause of action survives as specified under
-- src:981 | subsection (1) for the benefit of the estate of a deceased person,
-- src:982 | the damages recoverable for the benefit of the estate of that person —
-- src:991 | (b) in the case of a breach of promise to marry shall be limited
-- src:992 | to such damage, if any, to the estate of that person as flows
-- src:993 | from the breach of promise to marry;
@ref s 10(3)(b) (src:980-993)
GIVEN `the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of cause of action` IS A `Kind of cause of action`
      `the damage flows from the breach of promise to marry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3)(b) the damage is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a cause of action survives as specified under subsection (1) for the benefit of the estate"
        IF NOT (`the kind of cause of action` EQUALS `A claim for breach of promise to marry`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a breach of promise to marry"
        IF `the damage flows from the breach of promise to marry` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be limited to such damage, if any, to the estate of that person as flows from the breach of promise to marry"

-- src:980 | (3) Where a cause of action survives as specified under
-- src:981 | subsection (1) for the benefit of the estate of a deceased person,
-- src:982 | the damages recoverable for the benefit of the estate of that person —
-- src:995 | (c) where the death of that person has been caused by the act or
-- src:996 | omission which gives rise to the cause of action, shall be
-- src:997 | calculated without reference to any loss or gain to his estate
-- src:998 | consequent on his death except that a sum in respect of
-- src:999 | funeral expenses may be included.
@ref s 10(3)(c) (src:980-999)
GIVEN `the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the death was caused by the act or omission which gives rise to the cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is a sum in respect of funeral expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3)(c) the item is taken into account in calculating the damages` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a cause of action survives as specified under subsection (1) for the benefit of the estate"
        IF NOT `the death was caused by the act or omission which gives rise to the cause of action` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the death of that person has been caused by the act or omission which gives rise to the cause of action"
        IF `the item is a sum in respect of funeral expenses` THEN JUST TRUE -- "a sum in respect of funeral expenses may be included"
        IF `the item is a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be calculated without reference to any loss or gain to his estate consequent on his death"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an item that is neither consequent on the death nor funeral expenses is not addressed

-- src:1001 | (4) Where damage has been suffered by reason of any act or
-- src:1002 | omission in respect of which a cause of action would have subsisted
-- src:1003 | against any person if that person had not died before or at the same
-- src:1004 | time as the damage was suffered, there shall be deemed, for the
-- src:1005 | purposes of this section, to have been subsisting against him before
-- src:1006 | his death such cause of action in respect of that act or omission as
-- src:1007 | would have subsisted if he had died after the damage was suffered.
@ref s 10(4) (src:1001-1007)
GIVEN `damage has been suffered by reason of an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cause of action would have subsisted against the person in respect of it if he had not died before or at the same time as the damage was suffered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(4) the cause of action is deemed to have subsisted against the person before his death` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `damage has been suffered by reason of an act or omission` AND `a cause of action would have subsisted against the person in respect of it if he had not died before or at the same time as the damage was suffered` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where damage has been suffered by reason of any act or omission in respect of which a cause of action would have subsisted against any person if that person had not died before or at the same time as the damage was suffered, there shall be deemed ..." -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "where" is the text's no under the ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)

-- src:1009 | (5) The rights conferred by this section for the benefit of the estates
-- src:1010 | of deceased persons shall be in addition to and not in derogation of
-- src:1015 | any rights conferred on the dependants of deceased persons by
-- src:1016 | section 20 and so much of this section as relates to causes of action
-- src:1017 | against the estates of deceased persons shall apply in relation to
-- src:1018 | causes of action under that section as applies in relation to other
-- src:1019 | causes of action not expressly excepted from the operation of
-- src:1020 | subsection (1).
@ref s 10(5) (src:1009-1020)
GIVEN `the right is conferred by section 10 for the benefit of the estate of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) the rights of the estate take away from the rights of the dependants under section 20` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the right is conferred by section 10 for the benefit of the estate of a deceased person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be in addition to and not in derogation of any rights conferred on the dependants of deceased persons by section 20"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The rights conferred by this section for the benefit of the estates of deceased persons"

-- src:1015 | any rights conferred on the dependants of deceased persons by
-- src:1016 | section 20 and so much of this section as relates to causes of action
-- src:1017 | against the estates of deceased persons shall apply in relation to
-- src:1018 | causes of action under that section as applies in relation to other
-- src:1019 | causes of action not expressly excepted from the operation of
-- src:1020 | subsection (1).
@ref s 10(5) the application to causes of action under section 20 (src:1015-1020)
GIVEN `the cause of action is a cause of action against the estate of a deceased person under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause of action is expressly excepted from the operation of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) the part of section 10 on causes of action against estates applies to the cause of action under section 20` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cause of action is a cause of action against the estate of a deceased person under section 20` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so much of this section as relates to causes of action against the estates of deceased persons"
        IF `the cause of action is expressly excepted from the operation of subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as applies in relation to other causes of action not expressly excepted from the operation of subsection (1)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1022 | (6) In the event of the insolvency of an estate against which
-- src:1023 | proceedings are maintainable by virtue of this section, any liability in
-- src:1024 | respect of the cause of action in respect of which the proceedings are
-- src:1025 | maintainable shall be deemed to be a debt provable in the
-- src:1026 | administration of the estate, notwithstanding that it is a demand in
-- src:1027 | the nature of unliquidated damages arising otherwise than by a
-- src:1028 | contract, promise or breach of trust.
@ref s 10(6) (src:1022-1028)
GIVEN `the estate is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings are maintainable against the estate by virtue of section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(6) the liability is deemed a debt provable in the administration of the estate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the estate is insolvent` AND `proceedings are maintainable against the estate by virtue of section 10` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of the insolvency of an estate against which proceedings are maintainable by virtue of this section, any liability ... shall be deemed to be a debt provable" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "in the event of" is read as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b))

§ `Section 11 -- loss of expectation of life`

-- src:1032 | 11.—(1) In any action for damages for personal injuries, no
-- src:1033 | damages shall be recoverable in respect of any loss of expectation
-- src:1034 | of life caused to the injured person by the injuries, except that if the
-- src:1035 | injured person’s expectation of life has been reduced by the injuries,
@ref s 11(1) no damages (src:1032-1035)
GIVEN `the action is an action for damages for personal injuries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the damages are in respect of loss of income` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) damages are recoverable in respect of loss of expectation of life caused by the injuries` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is an action for damages for personal injuries` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any action for damages for personal injuries"
        IF `the damages are in respect of loss of income` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) says a reference to damages in respect of loss of expectation of life does not include damages in respect of loss of income, so subsection (1) does not reach them
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no damages shall be recoverable in respect of any loss of expectation of life caused to the injured person by the injuries"

-- src:1035 | injured person’s expectation of life has been reduced by the injuries,
-- src:1036 | the court, in assessing damages in respect of pain and suffering
-- src:1037 | caused by the injuries, shall take into account any suffering caused or
-- src:1038 | likely to be caused to him by awareness that his expectation of life has
-- src:1039 | been so reduced.
@ref s 11(1) the exception (src:1035-1039)
GIVEN `the action is an action for damages for personal injuries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person's expectation of life has been reduced by the injuries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the suffering is caused or likely to be caused by awareness that the expectation of life has been so reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) the court takes the suffering caused by awareness of the reduction into account in assessing damages for pain and suffering` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is an action for damages for personal injuries` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any action for damages for personal injuries"
        IF `the injured person's expectation of life has been reduced by the injuries` AND `the suffering is caused or likely to be caused by awareness that the expectation of life has been so reduced` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the injured person's expectation of life has been reduced by the injuries, the court ... shall take into account any suffering caused or likely to be caused to him by awareness that his expectation of life has been so reduced" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "if" is the text's no

-- src:1041 | (2) In subsection (1), any reference to damages in respect of loss of
-- src:1042 | expectation of life does not include damages in respect of loss of
-- src:1043 | income.
@ref s 11(2) (src:1041-1043)
GIVEN `the damages are in respect of loss of income` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) the damages are damages in respect of loss of expectation of life` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the damages are in respect of loss of income` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference to damages in respect of loss of expectation of life does not include damages in respect of loss of income"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what a reference does not include

§ `Section 12 -- interest on debts and damages`

-- src:1048 | 12.—(1) In any proceedings tried in any court of record for the
-- src:1049 | recovery of any debt or damages, the court may, if it thinks fit, order
-- src:1050 | that there shall be included in the sum for which judgment is given
-- src:1051 | interest at such rate as it thinks fit on the whole or any part of the debt
-- src:1052 | or damages for the whole or any part of the period between the date
-- src:1053 | when the cause of action arose and the date of the judgment.
@ref s 12(1) (src:1048-1053)
GIVEN `the proceedings are tried in a court of record for the recovery of a debt or damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(1) the court may order interest to be included in the sum for which judgment is given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are tried in a court of record for the recovery of a debt or damages` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings tried in any court of record for the recovery of any debt or damages"
        IF `the court thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may, if it thinks fit, order" -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "if" is the text's no

-- src:1051 | interest at such rate as it thinks fit on the whole or any part of the debt
-- src:1052 | or damages for the whole or any part of the period between the date
-- src:1053 | when the cause of action arose and the date of the judgment.
@ref s 12(1) the period (src:1051-1053)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the date when the cause of action arose` IS A DATE
      `the date of the judgment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(1) the day falls within the period for which interest may be ordered` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day` AT LEAST `the date when the cause of action arose` AND `the day` AT MOST `the date of the judgment` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the whole or any part of the period between the date when the cause of action arose and the date of the judgment" -- the period is fixed in the text's words (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a)); both endpoints are read as inside it (fork F-P1; the other reading is that an endpoint is outside)

-- src:1058 | (2) Nothing in this section —
-- src:1060 | (a) shall authorise the giving of interest upon interest;
@ref s 12(2)(a) (src:1058-1060)
GIVEN `the interest sought is interest upon interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2)(a) section 12 authorises the giving of the interest` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the interest sought is interest upon interest` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section — (a) shall authorise the giving of interest upon interest"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph takes interest upon interest out and says nothing of any other interest

-- src:1058 | (2) Nothing in this section —
-- src:1062 | (b) shall apply in relation to any debt upon which interest is
-- src:1063 | payable as of right whether by virtue of any agreement or
-- src:1064 | otherwise; or
@ref s 12(2)(b) (src:1058-1064)
GIVEN `interest is payable on the debt as of right whether by virtue of any agreement or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2)(b) section 12 applies in relation to the debt` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `interest is payable on the debt as of right whether by virtue of any agreement or otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section — ... (b) shall apply in relation to any debt upon which interest is payable as of right whether by virtue of any agreement or otherwise"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph takes a debt carrying interest as of right out and says nothing of any other debt

-- src:1058 | (2) Nothing in this section —
-- src:1066 | (c) shall affect the damages recoverable for the dishonour of a
-- src:1067 | bill of exchange.
@ref s 12(2)(c) (src:1058-1067)
GIVEN `the damages are damages recoverable for the dishonour of a bill of exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2)(c) section 12 affects the damages recoverable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the damages are damages recoverable for the dishonour of a bill of exchange` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section — ... (c) shall affect the damages recoverable for the dishonour of a bill of exchange"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the damages recoverable for the dishonour of a bill of exchange"

§ `Section 13 -- charges and mortgages over choses in action`

-- src:1071 | 13. For the avoidance of doubt, it is hereby declared that a person
-- src:1072 | (the first person) is able to create, and always has been able to create,
-- src:1073 | in favour of another person (the second person) a legal or equitable
-- src:1074 | charge or mortgage over all or any of the first person’s interest in a
-- src:1075 | chose in action enforceable by the first person against the second
@ref s 13 the declaration (src:1071-1075)
GIVEN `the chose in action is enforceable by the first person against the second person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge or mortgage is over all or any of the first person's interest in the chose in action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge or mortgage is created in favour of the second person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 the first person is able to create the charge or mortgage over the chose in action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the chose in action is enforceable by the first person against the second person` AND `the charge or mortgage is over all or any of the first person's interest in the chose in action` AND `the charge or mortgage is created in favour of the second person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a legal or equitable charge or mortgage over all or any of the first person's interest in a chose in action enforceable by the first person against the second person"

-- src:1075 | chose in action enforceable by the first person against the second
-- src:1076 | person, and any charge or mortgage so created shall operate neither to
-- src:1077 | merge the interest thereby created with, nor to extinguish or release,
-- src:1078 | that chose in action.
@ref s 13 no merger (src:1075-1078)
GIVEN `the charge or mortgage is one created as section 13 declares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 the charge or mortgage merges with or extinguishes or releases the chose in action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the charge or mortgage is one created as section 13 declares` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any charge or mortgage so created shall operate neither to merge the interest thereby created with, nor to extinguish or release, that chose in action"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any charge or mortgage so created"

§ `Section 14 -- husband's liability for wife's torts and antenuptial contracts, debts and obligations`

-- src:1083 | 14.—(1) Subject to this section, the husband of a married woman
-- src:1084 | shall not, by reason only of his being her husband, be liable —
-- src:1086 | (a) in respect of any tort committed by her whether before or
-- src:1087 | after the marriage, or in respect of any contract entered
-- src:1088 | into, or debt or obligation incurred, by her before the
-- src:1089 | marriage; or
@ref s 14(1)(a) (src:1083-1089)
GIVEN `the person is the husband of a married woman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is in respect of a tort committed by her whether before or after the marriage or a contract entered into or a debt or obligation incurred by her before the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability arises by reason only of his being her husband` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1)(a) the husband is liable in respect of the tort contract debt or obligation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is the husband of a married woman` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the husband of a married woman"
        IF `the liability is in respect of a tort committed by her whether before or after the marriage or a contract entered into or a debt or obligation incurred by her before the marriage` AND `the liability arises by reason only of his being her husband` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the husband of a married woman shall not, by reason only of his being her husband, be liable"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only of his being her husband": a liability on another footing is not addressed

-- src:1083 | 14.—(1) Subject to this section, the husband of a married woman
-- src:1084 | shall not, by reason only of his being her husband, be liable —
-- src:1091 | (b) to be sued or made a party to any legal proceedings brought
-- src:1092 | in respect of any such tort, contract, debt or obligation.
@ref s 14(1)(b) (src:1083-1092)
GIVEN `the person is the husband of a married woman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are brought in respect of a tort committed by her whether before or after the marriage or a contract entered into or a debt or obligation incurred by her before the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are brought against him by reason only of his being her husband` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1)(b) the husband may be sued or made a party to the legal proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is the husband of a married woman` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the husband of a married woman"
        IF `the proceedings are brought in respect of a tort committed by her whether before or after the marriage or a contract entered into or a debt or obligation incurred by her before the marriage` AND `the proceedings are brought against him by reason only of his being her husband` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not, by reason only of his being her husband, be liable ... to be sued or made a party to any legal proceedings"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only of his being her husband"

-- src:1094 | (2) For the avoidance of doubt, it is hereby declared that nothing in
-- src:1095 | this section —
-- src:1097 | (a) renders the husband of a married woman liable in respect
-- src:1098 | of any contract entered into, or debt or obligation incurred,
-- src:1099 | by her after the marriage in respect of which he would not
-- src:1100 | have been liable if this section had not been enacted;
@ref s 14(2)(a) (src:1094-1100)
GIVEN `the contract was entered into or the debt or obligation incurred by her after the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he would not have been liable in respect of it if section 14 had not been enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2)(a) section 14 renders the husband liable in respect of the contract debt or obligation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract was entered into or the debt or obligation incurred by her after the marriage` AND `he would not have been liable in respect of it if section 14 had not been enacted` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section — (a) renders the husband of a married woman liable in respect of any contract entered into, or debt or obligation incurred, by her after the marriage in respect of which he would not have been liable if this section had not been enacted"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names the contracts, debts and obligations after the marriage for which he would not have been liable

-- src:1094 | (2) For the avoidance of doubt, it is hereby declared that nothing in
-- src:1095 | this section —
-- src:1105 | (b) exempts the husband of a married woman from liability in
-- src:1106 | respect of any contract entered into, or debt or obligation
-- src:1107 | (not being a debt or obligation arising out of the
-- src:1108 | commission of a tort) incurred, by her after the marriage
-- src:1109 | in respect of which he would have been liable if this section
-- src:1110 | had not been enacted;
@ref s 14(2)(b) (src:1094-1110)
GIVEN `the contract was entered into or the debt or obligation (not arising out of the commission of a tort) incurred by her after the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he would have been liable in respect of it if section 14 had not been enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2)(b) section 14 exempts the husband from liability in respect of the contract debt or obligation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract was entered into or the debt or obligation (not arising out of the commission of a tort) incurred by her after the marriage` AND `he would have been liable in respect of it if section 14 had not been enacted` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section — ... (b) exempts the husband of a married woman from liability in respect of any contract entered into, or debt or obligation (not being a debt or obligation arising out of the commission of a tort) incurred, by her after the marriage in respect of which he would have been liable if this section had not been enacted"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names the contracts, debts and obligations after the marriage for which he would have been liable, and excludes a debt or obligation arising out of a tort

-- src:1094 | (2) For the avoidance of doubt, it is hereby declared that nothing in
-- src:1095 | this section —
-- src:1112 | (c) prevents a husband and wife from acquiring, holding and
-- src:1113 | disposing of, any property jointly or as tenants in common,
-- src:1114 | or from rendering themselves or being rendered jointly
-- src:1115 | liable in respect of any tort, contract, debt or obligation,
-- src:1116 | and of suing and being sued either in tort or in contract or
-- src:1117 | otherwise, in the like manner as if they were not married;
@ref s 14(2)(c) (src:1094-1117)
GIVEN `the act is acquiring holding or disposing of property jointly or as tenants in common or rendering themselves or being rendered jointly liable in respect of a tort contract debt or obligation or suing and being sued in tort or contract or otherwise in the like manner as if they were not married` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2)(c) section 14 prevents the husband and wife from the act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is acquiring holding or disposing of property jointly or as tenants in common or rendering themselves or being rendered jointly liable in respect of a tort contract debt or obligation or suing and being sued in tort or contract or otherwise in the like manner as if they were not married` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section — ... (c) prevents a husband and wife from acquiring, holding and disposing of, any property jointly or as tenants in common, or from rendering themselves or being rendered jointly liable ..., and of suing and being sued either in tort or in contract or otherwise, in the like manner as if they were not married"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph lists the acts it does not prevent

-- src:1094 | (2) For the avoidance of doubt, it is hereby declared that nothing in
-- src:1095 | this section —
-- src:1119 | (d) prevents the exercise of any joint power given to a husband
-- src:1120 | and wife.
@ref s 14(2)(d) (src:1094-1120)
GIVEN `the act is the exercise of a joint power given to a husband and wife` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2)(d) section 14 prevents the exercise of the joint power` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is the exercise of a joint power given to a husband and wife` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section — ... (d) prevents the exercise of any joint power given to a husband and wife"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any joint power given to a husband and wife"

§§ `Sections 10 to 14 -- tests`

-- s 10(1) and (2): a debt claim survives; the four causes of action do not
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the cause of action survives against or for the benefit of the estate` TRUE `Another cause of action` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "all causes of action ... shall survive"
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the cause of action survives against or for the benefit of the estate` TRUE `A claim for breach of promise to marry` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- survives (limited in damages by (3)(b))
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the cause of action survives against or for the benefit of the estate` TRUE Defamation EQUALS NOTHING -- "Subject to this section": see (2)
#ASSERT `s 10(1) the cause of action survives against or for the benefit of the estate` FALSE `Another cause of action` EQUALS NOTHING -- not a cause of action subsisting at death
#ASSERT `s 10(2) subsection (1) applies to the cause of action` Defamation EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "defamation"
#ASSERT `s 10(2) subsection (1) applies to the cause of action` Seduction EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "seduction"
#ASSERT `s 10(2) subsection (1) applies to the cause of action` `Inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other"
#ASSERT `s 10(2) subsection (1) applies to the cause of action` `A claim for damages on the ground of adultery` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "any claim for damages on the ground of adultery"
#ASSERT `s 10(2) subsection (1) applies to the cause of action` `Another cause of action` EQUALS NOTHING -- the subsection says nothing of any other
#ASSERT `s 10 the cause of action survives the death of the person` TRUE `Another cause of action` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- gathered: survives
#ASSERT `s 10 the cause of action survives the death of the person` TRUE Defamation EQUALS JUST FALSE -- gathered: (2) says no
#ASSERT `s 10 the cause of action survives the death of the person` FALSE `Another cause of action` EQUALS NOTHING -- gathered: nothing subsisted
-- s 10(3)
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(a) the head of damages is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` TRUE `Exemplary damages` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "any exemplary damages"
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(a) the head of damages is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` TRUE `Damages for loss of income in respect of a period after the death` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "any damages for loss of income in respect of any period after that person's death"
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(a) the head of damages is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` TRUE `Another head of damages` EQUALS NOTHING -- the paragraph says only what is not included
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(a) the head of damages is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` FALSE `Exemplary damages` EQUALS NOTHING -- the cause of action does not survive for the benefit of the estate
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(b) the damage is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` TRUE `A claim for breach of promise to marry` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- damage that flows from the breach
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(b) the damage is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` TRUE `A claim for breach of promise to marry` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "limited to such damage, if any, ... as flows from the breach"
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(b) the damage is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` TRUE `Another cause of action` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a breach of promise to marry
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(c) the item is taken into account in calculating the damages` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- funeral expenses "may be included"
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(c) the item is taken into account in calculating the damages` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "without reference to any loss or gain to his estate consequent on his death"
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(c) the item is taken into account in calculating the damages` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an item the paragraph does not address
#ASSERT `s 10(3)(c) the item is taken into account in calculating the damages` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the death was not caused by the act or omission
-- s 10(4) to (6)
#ASSERT `s 10(4) the cause of action is deemed to have subsisted against the person before his death` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the deeming
#ASSERT `s 10(4) the cause of action is deemed to have subsisted against the person before his death` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no cause of action would have subsisted: "Where"
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the rights of the estate take away from the rights of the dependants under section 20` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "in addition to and not in derogation of"
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the rights of the estate take away from the rights of the dependants under section 20` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a right under section 10
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the part of section 10 on causes of action against estates applies to the cause of action under section 20` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- applies as to other causes of action
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the part of section 10 on causes of action against estates applies to the cause of action under section 20` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- expressly excepted from (1)
#ASSERT `s 10(5) the part of section 10 on causes of action against estates applies to the cause of action under section 20` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a cause of action under section 20 against an estate
#ASSERT `s 10(6) the liability is deemed a debt provable in the administration of the estate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be deemed to be a debt provable"
#ASSERT `s 10(6) the liability is deemed a debt provable in the administration of the estate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the estate is not insolvent: "In the event of the insolvency"
-- s 11
#ASSERT `s 11(1) damages are recoverable in respect of loss of expectation of life caused by the injuries` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "no damages shall be recoverable"
#ASSERT `s 11(1) damages are recoverable in respect of loss of expectation of life caused by the injuries` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- loss of income: see (2)
#ASSERT `s 11(1) damages are recoverable in respect of loss of expectation of life caused by the injuries` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an action for personal injuries
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the court takes the suffering caused by awareness of the reduction into account in assessing damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall take into account"
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the court takes the suffering caused by awareness of the reduction into account in assessing damages for pain and suffering` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- expectation of life not reduced: "if"
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the court takes the suffering caused by awareness of the reduction into account in assessing damages for pain and suffering` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a personal injuries action
#ASSERT `s 11(2) the damages are damages in respect of loss of expectation of life` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "does not include damages in respect of loss of income"
#ASSERT `s 11(2) the damages are damages in respect of loss of expectation of life` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the subsection says what a reference does not include
-- s 12: the period is tested on both sides of each end
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the court may order interest to be included in the sum for which judgment is given` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may, if it thinks fit, order"
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the court may order interest to be included in the sum for which judgment is given` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the court does not think fit
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the court may order interest to be included in the sum for which judgment is given` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not proceedings in a court of record for a debt or damages
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the day falls within the period for which interest may be ordered` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day the cause of action arose
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the day falls within the period for which interest may be ordered` (Date 28 2 2025) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day before the cause of action arose
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the day falls within the period for which interest may be ordered` (Date 30 6 2025) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day of the judgment
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the day falls within the period for which interest may be ordered` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day after the judgment
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(a) section 12 authorises the giving of the interest` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall authorise the giving of interest upon interest"
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(a) section 12 authorises the giving of the interest` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another interest
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(b) section 12 applies in relation to the debt` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- interest payable as of right
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(b) section 12 applies in relation to the debt` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another debt
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(c) section 12 affects the damages recoverable` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- dishonour of a bill of exchange
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(c) section 12 affects the damages recoverable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- other damages
-- s 13
#ASSERT `s 13 the first person is able to create the charge or mortgage over the chose in action` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the declaration
#ASSERT `s 13 the first person is able to create the charge or mortgage over the chose in action` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a chose in action not enforceable against the second person
#ASSERT `s 13 the first person is able to create the charge or mortgage over the chose in action` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- in favour of a third person
#ASSERT `s 13 the charge or mortgage merges with or extinguishes or releases the chose in action` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "neither to merge ... nor to extinguish or release"
#ASSERT `s 13 the charge or mortgage merges with or extinguishes or releases the chose in action` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a charge not so created
-- s 14
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(a) the husband is liable in respect of the tort contract debt or obligation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not, by reason only of his being her husband, be liable"
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(a) the husband is liable in respect of the tort contract debt or obligation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a liability on another footing
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(a) the husband is liable in respect of the tort contract debt or obligation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not the husband of a married woman
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(b) the husband may be sued or made a party to the legal proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "to be sued or made a party to any legal proceedings"
#ASSERT `s 14(1)(b) the husband may be sued or made a party to the legal proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- proceedings in respect of another matter
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(a) section 14 renders the husband liable in respect of the contract debt or obligation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "nothing in this section renders the husband ... liable"
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(a) section 14 renders the husband liable in respect of the contract debt or obligation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- he would have been liable anyway
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(b) section 14 exempts the husband from liability in respect of the contract debt or obligation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "nothing in this section exempts"
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(b) section 14 exempts the husband from liability in respect of the contract debt or obligation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a debt arising out of a tort
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(c) section 14 prevents the husband and wife from the act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "nothing in this section prevents"
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(c) section 14 prevents the husband and wife from the act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another act
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(d) section 14 prevents the exercise of the joint power` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "prevents the exercise of any joint power"
#ASSERT `s 14(2)(d) section 14 prevents the exercise of the joint power` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another power
